  "rationale": "Every row scored **Mechanical** claims a fail-closed check already enforces it. Nothing witnesses that claim: gz validate --advisory-scorecard checks that each rule is scored at its current version, never that the cited gate catches a violation of THAT row. The enforcement-floor negative controls are the repo mutation witness, but they are SCOPE-granular while these rows are PROPERTY-granular: 64 rows cite 46 distinct validator flags, 6 flags carry 2-3 rows each, and one scope routinely enforces several properties. Demonstrated 2026-08-10: --instructions-files-budget is cited by two Mechanical rows and has a live negative control that plants a per-file char-budget violation; it passed green the entire time the must-survive delivery predicate of the same scope was broken (fixed f9e9a4618). Scope-level coverage would have scored that row witnessed. Five Mechanical rows were found false in the two days before this freeze. Operator ruling 2026-08-10: ratchet forward - a row NEWLY scored or RE-SCORED Mechanical must cite a property-level negative control as NC:<claim-id>; the rows below are frozen as today debt and the list may only shrink. Keys are <section-id>#<row> because bare row numbers are NOT unique - 31 of them appear twice across the three tables, so every prior ruling citing a bare row number is an ambiguous reference.",
  "gates_step": "advisory scorecard mechanical-row witness (gz validate --advisory-scorecard)",
